    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I implemented `run_tool` in `opsbot/calls.py`. The 3 existing tests pass, and I also tried it against a real in-memory MCP server.\n\n```python\ndef _text(result: CallToolResult) -> str:\n    return \"\\n\".join(block.text for block in result.content if isinstance(block, TextContent))\n\n\nasync def run_tool(session: ClientSession, name: str, arguments: dict[str, Any]) -> Any:\n    \"\"\"Call tool `name` and return its structured output, or else its text.\"\"\"\n    result = await session.call_tool(name, arguments)\n    if result.is_error:\n        raise ToolCallFailed(name, _text(result))\n    # Any JSON value can be structured output (including 0, \"\" or []), so test for None.\n    if result.structured_content is not None:\n        return result.structured_content\n    return _text(result)\n```\n\n**Details:**\n- In mcp 2.2.0 the result fields are `is_error` and `structured_content`, not the older `isError` / `structuredContent`.\n- Structured output can be any JSON value in this version, including falsy ones like `0`, `\"\"` or `[]`. So I check `is not None` rather than truthiness. Otherwise a tool returning `0` would wrongly fall back to text.\n- Only text blocks go into the message or return value. Other block types (images, resources) are skipped.\n- Protocol-level errors, such as an unknown tool, are not `ToolCallFailed`. They are raised by the SDK as before.\n\n**What the server test showed:**\n- A tool returning text came back as `'hi x'`.\n- A tool with an `int` return came back as structured output `{'result': 0}`. The server wraps it that way.\n- A tool with a bare `-> dict` return has no structured output in this SDK version. The server sends it as JSON text, so `run_tool` returns that text. The CLI will print that JSON string as-is instead of re-formatting it with sorted keys.\n- A failing tool raised `ToolCallFailed('boom', 'Error executing tool boom: no such version')`. The server adds the \"Error executing tool \u2026\" prefix itself.\n\n**Cleanup needed:** the permission settings wouldn't let me "
